- Yeah! You're... You're stealing our pitch.

459
00:18:29,919 --> 00:18:31,878
- Are you stealing it?
- And you're Gilligan?

460
00:18:31,879 --> 00:18:34,464
Uh, well, that actually tracks
because she's got the same body...

461
00:18:34,465 --> 00:18:35,549
- Yes.
- ...but I don't love it.

462
00:18:35,550 --> 00:18:37,759
This is bullshit. Have you guys
been working on this for years?

463
00:18:37,760 --> 00:18:40,429
Well, we couldn't pitch
the episode idea with you guys.

464
00:18:40,430 --> 00:18:43,018
Because you guys are all into
conspiracy theories and stuff.

465
00:18:43,018 --> 00:18:44,641
- Constantly.
- There was a conspiracy.

466
00:18:44,642 --> 00:18:46,226
You had us locked in the par--

467
00:18:46,227 --> 00:18:47,769
- Give me the hat.
- Stop it.

468
00:18:47,770 --> 00:18:49,855
I'll tell you what, get your own hat.
Get your own hat.

469
00:18:49,856 --> 00:18:51,773
- Hey, hey! Stop!
- Okay. All right, all right.

470
00:18:53,543 --> 00:18:55,610
So anyway, so, um...

471
00:18:55,611 --> 00:18:58,113
So anyway, the Professor, uh,
realizes that he can use

472
00:18:58,114 --> 00:19:00,991
the same wheelbarrow technology
to create a boat, and I... you get it.

473
00:19:00,992 --> 00:19:02,451
What do you think, man?

474
00:19:02,452 --> 00:19:04,744
Well, this is great.
I would love to see this episode.

475
00:19:04,745 --> 00:19:06,121
- Really?
- You would?

476
00:19:06,122 --> 00:19:07,289
- Oh, wow.
- Wait.

477
00:19:07,290 --> 00:19:09,082
Well, this would require
some back-end compensation.

478
00:19:09,083 --> 00:19:10,167
Of course.

479
00:19:10,168 --> 00:19:11,251
Okay, so, uh, how's this work?

480
00:19:11,252 --> 00:19:12,711
You fly us out to Hollywood

481
00:19:12,712 --> 00:19:14,505
or you want to put us in touch
with your agent or...

482
00:19:15,131 --> 00:19:16,506
My agent?

483
00:19:16,507 --> 00:19:18,133
- Or your grandfather's agent.
- His grandfather's agent.

484
00:19:18,134 --> 00:19:19,217
I mean, yeah.

485
00:19:19,218 --> 00:19:21,636
Oh, I'm so sorry.
I-I think I see the confusion here.

486
00:19:21,637 --> 00:19:24,223
<i>I'm not related
to the creator of Gilligan's Island.</i>

487
00:19:24,974 --> 00:19:26,433
W... What?

488
00:19:26,434 --> 00:19:28,810
You got the same last name.
We looked you up.

489
00:19:28,811 --> 00:19:30,520
- We did our own research.
- Yeah.

490
00:19:30,521 --> 00:19:32,397
There's some confusion online.
People have mixed us up before.

491
00:19:32,398 --> 00:19:34,399
My grandfather is also named
Sherwood Schwartz,

492
00:19:34,400 --> 00:19:36,109
but he owns a Laundromat in Albany.

493
00:19:36,110 --> 00:19:38,278
- Dude.
- Oh, goddamn you. Goddamn you!

494
00:19:38,279 --> 00:19:39,905
What are you doing here
listening to our pitch

495
00:19:39,906 --> 00:19:41,490
if you're not even related to the guy?

496
00:19:41,491 --> 00:19:43,533
I'm sorry, but you seemed so passionate
when you approached me,

497
00:19:43,534 --> 00:19:44,910
and I didn't want to let you down.

498
00:19:44,911 --> 00:19:47,746
I mean, thank you for this, and, you know,

499
00:19:47,747 --> 00:19:49,873
it is a shame they didn't get
a hundredth episode.

500
00:19:49,874 --> 00:19:51,041
- You lousy basta--
- Oh, shut up!

501
00:19:51,042 --> 00:19:52,626
- Get outta here!
- Get outta here, man!

502
00:19:52,627 --> 00:19:54,169
You don't get to say that.
Shut up! Shut up!

503
00:19:54,170 --> 00:19:56,505
- Damn it!
- What a goddamn waste of time!

504
00:19:56,506 --> 00:19:59,090
Yeah. Wow, we really got worked up, huh?

505
00:19:59,091 --> 00:20:01,510
Well, we probably shouldn't be believing
everything we read online.

506
00:20:01,511 --> 00:20:03,512
- Oh, yeah.
- Maybe not everything is a conspiracy.

507
00:20:03,513 --> 00:20:06,389
Guys, we can't just attribute meaning
where there just isn't any.

508
00:20:06,390 --> 00:20:10,227
I mean, sometimes, guys,
there just is no "there" there.

509
00:20:11,896 --> 00:20:15,106
Hey, I got it,
an ending that's gonna make Grandpa proud.

510
00:20:15,107 --> 00:20:17,359
The world's finally gonna get
all the answers.

511
00:20:17,360 --> 00:20:19,069
Wait till everybody sees this.

512
00:20:19,529 --> 00:20:21,280
Too bad they never will.

